# src

`src/` contains application routes, components, and shared data behavior.

Code instantiated and used exclusively by a child feature belongs with that owner, including feature-local singletons. Instance count alone does not justify application-wide ownership. Preserve per-request server state.

## Ownership rules

Keep the existing React layout: application-wide and reusable data modules both use `lib/`; UI modules both use `components/`. Audit their placement against existing route directories and the auth/database child boundaries. Flat route files are not separate folder owners. Framework route entry points, generated database schemas, and portable registry sources are not relocation candidates. Registry consumers outside this project cannot be inferred from local usage. Coverage warnings and suggested destinations require review before any move into a TanStack route directory; helpers there must follow the router's ignored-file conventions. This rule update enables checks without requesting file moves.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "data-ownership",
      "match": "lib/**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "exclude": [
        "lib/db/schema/**"
      ],
      "ownership": {
        "core": "lib",
        "shared": "lib",
        "owners": [
          "routes/*",
          "lib/auth",
          "lib/db"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ui-ownership",
      "match": "components/**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "exclude": [
        "components/structures/**"
      ],
      "ownership": {
        "core": "components",
        "shared": "components",
        "owners": [
          "routes/*"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

documentation.structures-src-components:
# components

`src/components/` contains UI extracted for reuse or a meaningful independent responsibility, including profile integration and explorer composition. `structure-explorer.tsx` composes shared tree and Markdown components for the website; `structures/structure-explorer.tsx` exposes the portable component API.

## Module naming rules

Executable filename conventions for this folder; preserve dot suffixes for tests and declarations.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "module-names",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "case": "kebab-case"
    }
  ]
}
```

